──────
  ## AgriShield: Complete Audit Report
  ──────
  ### 🔴 TOTAL BLUNDERS — Will crash or block your demo

  1. Auth blocks the entire app.
  App.tsx wraps every page in a ProtectedRoute that redirects to /login if there's no Supabase session. Your Supabase URL is a real project     
  (ixtgiczwnmjjfjekloda.supabase.co) but there are no users created. The first thing a judge sees is a login screen. They can't get in. The     
  whole demo is blocked behind a wall.

  2. MarketObservation has no location_id.
  The model stores market_id, but main.py line 97 queries using MarketObservation.location_id which doesn't exist on the model. The history     
  chart in the Alert Detail page will throw a 500 error or return empty every single time. This is a silent database crash.

  3. get_alert in main.py will crash on missing alerts.
  Line 74: alert, location, commodity = db.query(...).first() — if .first() returns None, this unpacking crashes Python with a TypeError.       
  There's no null check. Any invalid URL like /alert/999 crashes the server.

  4. The recommended_action field is never set by the engine.
  engine.py never assigns alert.recommended_action. So alert.recommended_action in the UI renders as blank/undefined. The entire "Recommended   
  Action" black card on the detail page is empty.

  5. The explanation is auto-generated garbage.
  Line 171: "Anomaly score 84.0. Based on 3 signals." — this is what judges will read. It tells them nothing meaningful. It is not a
  demonstration of intelligence.
  ──────
  ### 🟠 MAJOR ISSUES — Broken features that will embarrass you
  6. Auth is connected to a real Supabase project but with no database schema.
  The backend .env has DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./agrishield.db (local SQLite). The frontend connects to real Supabase auth. These two systems    
  are completely disconnected. The JWT from Supabase is never verified by FastAPI (the auth.py verify_token function exists but is not
  applied to any route). Auth is both broken AND pointless.

  7. The AlertSignal join in main.py is fragile.
  The signals join in get_alerts (line 61) does from app.models import AlertSignal inside the loop. This re-imports on every iteration. More    
  importantly, if seed.py is re-run (which drops and recreates all tables), the AlertSignal table is cleared but signals are regenerated from   
  scratch — the alert IDs won't match the old signal IDs, causing the Overview cards to show empty bars.

  8. The Map component has no fallback when latitude/longitude is null.
  seed.py gives locations real coordinates, but if any location has null, Leaflet crashes the entire React app with an unhandled error. There   
  is a conditional render but Leaflet's map container itself can break.

  9. The ingest_news.py / ingest_satellite.py scripts require API keys that you don't have.
  In DEMO_MODE=True, ingest_ogd.py falls back to fixtures. But checking ingest_news.py — it requires a GEMINI_API_KEY. DEMO_MODE is not
  consistently checked in all three scripts. If a judge or you run run_all_ingestions.py, it will crash with a missing key error.
  10. seed.py has a bug: arrival_quantity is random 500–1000 for ALL locations including the "anomaly" one.
  The anomaly was only seeded on price and satellite signals for Nashik Onion. The arrival_quantity on the anomaly days is still random-        
  normal. The engine's arrival signal for Nashik Onion will show no anomaly, which contradicts the price spike. The story the dashboard tells   
  is internally inconsistent.
  ──────
  ### 🟡 MODERATE ISSUES — Things that look broken or confuse judges

  11. Loading states are just "Loading..." plain text.
  The loading spinner is <div className="text-primary text-xl">Loading...</div>. On a white background with no animation, this looks like a     
  crashed page.
  12. Alert cards show risk_score.toFixed(1) but some alerts will have risk_score = null.
  For location/commodity combos with no data, evaluate_alert returns None. Those alerts are never inserted. But if the data is partially        
  there, risk_score could be 0, which .toFixed(1) renders as "0.0" — confusing.

  13. The Methodology page is static text with no live numbers.
  There are no real numbers from your actual engine run. No "In our test, Nashik Onion reached 84.2 with price deviation of +27%." It's just    
  generic description. It's a missed opportunity to wow judges with real evidence.

  14. mockData.ts is still imported in AlertDetail.tsx (even though mockHistory/mockTimeline were removed, the file still exists and is
  technically dead code).
  15. The "Demo Mode" badge in the nav says "Demo Mode" always, regardless of the .env flag.
  It never actually reads DEMO_MODE from the backend.

  16. The recommended_action field in seed.py and engine.py is never populated, so the bold "Recommended Action" card on every Alert Detail     
  is completely blank.
  ──────
  ### 🟢 WHAT ACTUALLY WORKS (Don't Touch)

  • The engine.py math is solid — deviation, normalization, weight renormalization, consistency score.
  • seed.py generates a believable anomaly for Nashik Onion correctly for price and satellite.
  • The Overview.tsx accordion expand/collapse with signal bars is sharp and works well.
  • npm run build compiles with zero TypeScript errors.
  • Methodology.tsx content is accurate and professionally written.
  • The Map component displays correctly when coordinates exist.
  • The database schema (models.py) is well-designed and clean.
  ──────
  ### The Minimum Viable Fix List to Win

  If you do only these things, the project goes from "crashy prototype" to "impressive demo":

  1. Remove auth entirely or bypass it for the demo (one line change — hardcode session = true).
  2. Fix the MarketObservation.location_id query in main.py (join through Market table instead).
  3. Fix the .first() crash in get_alert with a null check.
  4. Add real recommended_action and explanation text in engine.py based on which signals fired.
  5. Fix arrival_quantity in seed.py to show a drop during the anomaly period for Nashik Onion.
  6. Add a loading spinner (one Tailwind class).